@snnh/dsh-llm-service-lite README · Further Exploration：- [LLM streaming subsystem](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/blob/master/docs/subsystems/llm-streaming.md) — the message and block types, the assembled request, and the adapter contract this package implements.
- [Providers guide](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/blob/master/docs/user/guide/providers.md) — how a deployment configures providers on the shipped profiles.
- [OpenWebCode](https://github.com/snnh/openwebcode) — the provider-profile model this adapter follows.

@snnh/dsh-llm-service-lite README · Known Limitations and Deferred Work：- **Three protocols, three shapes.** Every declared protocol has a transport, and each carries that protocol's own features: the Responses API's server-side tools (`web_search_call` items) are not carried, and no `store` field is sent, so a deployment keeps provider-side state out of the request path.
- **Configuration lives on the Models page seats, the plugin page, or in the patch.** The plugin fills the Models page's adapter-family extension seats and the bundle's page under **Plugins**; the profile's `cordis.patch.yml` remains the surface for hand-written fields the editors do not render (see [Mount](#mount)).
- **Video input arrives as a file, not as moving pictures.** A declared `video` input is carried as the file handle every attachment contributes, because no wire here has a video part and the harness has no video content block yet. `image` input is carried, and so is the token accounting a profile declares through `imageTokens`; a route that declares none keeps the meter's structural heuristic, and no adapter-authored handle text travels beside the bytes, so a priced occurrence counts the visual token

